  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since $(x-2)^{3}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x$ for large values of $x,$ the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{(x-2)^{3}}=0.\n$$",
